{
    "background_story": "Ryatt was a young Apache warrior who lived in the vast expanse of the American Southwest. Growing up, he learned the traditional ways of his people from his wise and aged grandfather, Grey Wolf. One of the most valuable lessons Ryatt learned was how to build a sturdy wickiup, a traditional Apache dwelling made from branches and thatched with leaves. Ryatt's skills as a wickiup builder were unmatched, and his structures could withstand the harsh desert winds and rains. When his tribe was forced to flee their ancestral lands, Ryatt's knowledge of wickiup construction proved invaluable, providing shelter and protection for his people. His expertise earned him the respect and admiration of his tribe, and he became known as a master builder and a keeper of Apache traditions.",
